WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.759
Another type of wireless network is a cellular
network, which most mobile devices run on.

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:11.110
The highest speed cellular network is 5G though
that network is not available in every area

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.980
nor on every mobile device at this time.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.360
Most mobile devices have access to 4G or 4G
LTE, Long-Term Evolution networks, a faster

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.380
version of 4G networks.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.300
Some mobile devices only have access to 3G
or 2G networks.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.300
One item to note on mobile device networks
is that speeds vary greatly based on the proximity

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.480
of a mobile device to a tower.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.230
Depending upon one's cellular service plan,
one's speeds could be throttled during peak

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:41.940
hours or if a cellular customer exceeds a
certain amount of used bandwidth per billing

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.260
period.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.770
Satellite is another type of internet connection
that is prominent in areas to where is no

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.120
cable or DSL internet availability and cell
service is not consistent.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.160
Satellite internet is generally faster than
dial-up but the biggest issue with satellites

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:02.250
is latency, the delay from a source to a destination,
as a signal needs to travel up to 20,000 miles

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.489
above the Earth and then back down to a destination.

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:09.860
For that reason, satellite internet is not
the best for real-time activities such as

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.360
video conferencing and gaming.

